---
// Home (site design §6): what OME is, its games and their support levels, where to get it and the games.
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import ome from 'virtual:ome';

const releases = `${ome.repository}/releases/latest`;
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Open Maid Engine',
		template: 'splash',
		head: [{ tag: 'title', content: 'Open Maid Engine' }],
		hero: {
			tagline: 'An open reimplementation of AGE, the engine of Eushully’s games, built for modding.',
			actions: [
				{ text: 'Read the modding guide', link: '/docs/', icon: 'right-arrow' },
				{ text: 'Get OME', link: releases, icon: 'external', variant: 'minimal' },
			],
		},
	}}
>
	<h2>What it is</h2>
	<p>
		Open Maid Engine (OME) runs Eushully’s games from your own copy of them. No game file is part of OME: you supply
		an installed game, and OME reads it. It runs on Windows and Linux, and it is free software under the MIT License.
	</p>
	<p>
		Modding comes first. A mod is a package that patches a game’s scripts, adds scenes and assets, translates the
		game’s text, runs Lua beside its scripts or changes its data tables. Script mods also export to the original
		engine; translations, Lua and data files run in OME.
	</p>

	<h2>The games</h2>
	<p>
		Each game has two support levels. Play says how well OME runs it, from P1 (OME reads the game) to P4 (verified
		against the original to its ending). Modding says what a modder gets, from M1 (script mods) to M3 (a base mod for
		Lua and data files). <a href="/docs/games/">The supported games</a> page explains each level.
	</p>
	<table class="ome-games">
		<thead>
			<tr><th>Game</th><th>Play</th><th>Modding</th><th>Modding guide</th><th>The game</th></tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			{
				ome.games.map((game) => (
					<tr>
						<td>{game.title}</td>
						<td>{game.play ?? '—'}</td>
						<td>{game.modding ?? '—'}</td>
						<td><a href={`/docs/games/${game.id}/`}>{game.id}</a></td>
						<td>{game.site ? <a href={game.site}>The maker’s site</a> : '—'}</td>
					</tr>
				))
			}
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2>Get OME</h2>
	<p>
		OME’s releases are on <a href={releases}>GitHub</a>, with packages for Windows and Linux. Each carries a
		launcher, which keeps a profile for each game you play, with its mods.
	</p>

	<h2>The game database</h2>
	<p>
		A page for each item, unit and skill of a game, mined from the game by OME: Kamidori Alchemy Meister first.
		It is not built yet.
	</p>
</StarlightPage>
